# Noetica (ENG-268). Upstream ships no .gitattributes, so on a default Windows clone
# (core.autocrlf=true) the generation inputs arrive as CRLF — and sofia's awk splits its
# templates on form-feed + LF with BINMODE=rw. Nothing then matches the record separator
# and the scripts produce empty or garbled output *while exiting 0*, with no error.
#
# These rules make the LF requirement a property of the checkout rather than an
# instruction someone has to have read. The CI workflow still sets core.autocrlf=false
# and asserts the result; that is now belt-and-braces instead of the only defence.
#
# Scope is deliberately the generation inputs, not the whole tree: a blanket rule would
# rewrite every file in an upstream fork and make merges from freeswitch/sofia-sip noisy.

*.awk           text eol=lf
*.in            text eol=lf
configure.ac    text eol=lf

# Read by build_sources.cmd alongside the .h.in templates.
libsofia-sip-ua/sip/sip_extra_headers.txt   text eol=lf
libsofia-sip-ua/sip/sip_bad_mask            text eol=lf

# The .cmd scripts are run by cmd.exe, which is happy either way; left alone so they
# match whatever upstream ships.
